From 04e9fe6c85b680c2f8e29c22e084dab6012babbe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Han <danielhanchen@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 06:48:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ggml : fused value-preserving ops for adaLN DiT blocks

Three ops that replace long chains of elementwise ops, copies and concats in
diffusion transformers such as MiniMax-H3 while producing the same bits as the
chains they replace (every product, sum, scale and conversion is rounded
separately, never contracted into an FMA):

- ggml_rope_pe_permute: rotary embedding with a precomputed [cos, -sin; sin,
  cos] table on the first n_rot channels (non-interleaved pairing), pass-through
  for the rest, written in the head-major [d, tokens, heads] layout attention
  reads, with an optional scale and F16 cast. Reads a strided view, so the
  q/k/v chunks of a fused qkv projection need no copies.
- ggml_modulate_rows / ggml_gated_add_rows: (x + x*scale) + shift and
  base + u*gate on a row range, written in place into an accumulator so a
  sequence split into segments with different modulation vectors needs no
  slice copies and no concat. Optional output / input scale.
- ggml_swiglu_scaled: silu(s_in*a) * (s_in*b) scaled by s_out, i.e. a Linear
  output scale, swiglu and the next Linear input scale in one pass.

CPU and CUDA implementations; other backends report the ops unsupported so
callers keep their unfused graphs. test-backend-ops covers strided inputs,
partial and full rotation, F32/F16 outputs, chained segments and the scales.
---
